What this says about a rewrite:

Reassociating a sum, or fusing a*b + a*c into a*(b+c), is licensed by
a law. The law is a property of the POLICY, not of the operation and
not of the width. So the same source expression admits a fused kernel
under one policy and does not under another, with everything else
held identical. That is I9 stated as something checkable rather than
as a slogan: the strategy is what makes an answer correct, because it
is what decides which rewrites preserve the answer.
